        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2a8a53a1ae1340e0acc418bbb15084c0",
      "statement": "Release is read-then-conditional-write: release_owner blanks the record only when it still names this node at this epoch, treats a takeover as an ordinary outcome rather than an error, and never strips a new live owner's claim.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L379-L398",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dda607b00f77e8f776a6295ce6de2bfdeb42d69ab18c2930127ef178c6ab2c4c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d2b1dc62a89a4393816f396c54b495c8",
      "statement": "Every activation (takeover or local wake) advances the epoch; each owner replicates under cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/ with unconditional PUTs, and the epoch in the key is the fence: a node that lost ownership writes into a superseded prefix that no restore selects, so an epoch never has two writers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L114-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4266403b34060864e7dce422b45ba3bc833b3bbf5aa09321b0af00e113fbdb82:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_243aecdc4df04d8e90de05ecd1667396",
      "statement": "Cell-scope naming is itself a security fence: a scope becomes a path component and replication key, so it is restricted to ASCII alphanumerics plus `_ - . : $` and bounded at MAX_CELL_SCOPE=255 bytes, rejecting `.` and `..` so it cannot escape the data directory or the bucket prefix.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/cell.rs#L1-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e052387002c201701695c5920d9e66adee69f30cf7d7404af2dae20fe6020b20:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1683c764c49a48e1a127de47af89a344",
      "statement": "Node leases carry an expiry in nodes/<node>.json; renewal is paced at one-third of CELLD_TTL_MS (default 10000 ms), a failed renewal does not fence the node while the published expiry stands, and a node whose lease expires or whose record was replaced fences itself — stopping active cells and failing incomplete requests without writing anything to the bucket.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/actor.rs#L2091-L2091",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72babfc4799ca7410708fd2bc807ab5df591f014264ab77509e312e89b0bf8b1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/machine.rs#L54-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0945233e3ca7834010d4f027a6a08a9e7f609f2bd96d6abdcba0bf678a3b3061:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L197-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64a09f9bb8c05f0b4688477dbbafa30f0bf7ec46fadb97ffb93e500d7e056b8a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_424a23f5414548dcbecfadd0168666d2",
      "statement": "Self-fencing emits a `SELF-FENCE:` log line naming the cause and exits with code 3 via exit_flushed (log-guard drop then std::process::exit); other internal failures use the same prefix and code; the fenced state is terminal and only a restart returns the node to the fleet.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L118-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2b0fbead6349a6344a7a991fa33d524f5529915076e093991a529ccc011ddf5:"
        },
